+## 0.3.0 (2026-10-18)
+
+Breaking (minor bump for 0.x; no crate in this workspace depends on rightkit-device):
+- `AuthorizationDenial` is now `#[non_exhaustive]` and gains `Revoked { id }` and `Refused(String)`. A revoked-id outcome needs its own variant (the app must tell "revoked" from "invalid"); no additive encoding exists. Exhaustive matches in apps need a wildcard arm.
+
+Added:
+- `AuthorizationService::with_revoked_ids(RevokedIds)` / `set_revoked_ids`: `authorize` now verifies with `rightkit_license::verify_token_not_revoked`, so a token whose entitlement id is on the app's list is denied with `Revoked { id }`, ahead of expiry (rightkit#728). The default is an empty list, so existing callers behave as before. `RevokedIds` is re-exported.
+- `AuthorizationService::with_hashed_device_id()` and `with_device_alternates(ids)`: accept a token bound to the raw device id, its `device_id_hash`, or any listed id; the signature is verified once (`verify_token_any_device`, rightkit#610). Requires `rightkit-license` 0.2.2.
+- Feature `credentials`: `CredentialStore<T>`, a `SecureStore` over one account of `rightkit_credentials::Store` (OS keychain; nothing is written to files), with `strings` and `with_codec` constructors and native create-only `set_if_absent` (rightkit#748).
+- Tests for revocation, alternate device ids and the hashed candidate.
+
